WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.267
Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.167
You're here. You made it.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.701
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.234
Guys, I want to wish everyone a Happy Fallon-tine's Day.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:14.934
[ Cheers and applause ] That's what it is.

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.968
Happy Valentine's Day, everybody.

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:18.834
You can tell it's Valentine's Day

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:21.667
because CVS just put out all their Easter candy.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.000
Yeah, that's...

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.033
Of course, a lot of people celebrated tonight

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:26.634
with a romantic dinner.

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:28.701
And for everyone who tried making a reservation

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.667
on OpenTable today, it just says,

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.033
"Everything is booked. Call Uber Eats."

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:33.667
That's interesting.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.033
Well, this is going viral.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:37.133
A restaurant in Belgium has come up with a unique way

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:39.367
of serving customers their pasta on this day.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:40.634
Take a look at this.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:49.000
♪♪

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:55.767
After watching that, Stanley Tucci

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.934
locked himself in a closet and cried.

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:01.167
I don't want to brag, but when I'm out with my wife,

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.734
we like to order the whole bottle of pasta.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:06.701
No big deal.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:08.801
Get this. I ready that 52% of Americans

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.200
plan to celebrate Valentine's Day today

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.901
and spend an average of $192.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:16.400
You know, they release this kind of data every Valentine's Day.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.133
It's very interesting here. Take a look at some other stats.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:23.000
When it comes to dates, 20% of couples go to a nice restaurant,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.434
20% go to the movies,

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:27.100
while 60% go in the backyard

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.167
and shoot down UFOs together.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.968
It's a thing that people are doing.

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:33.200
"Right there, honey!"

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.267
[ Applause ]

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:35.601
-Whoo!

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:38.767
-Up next, when it comes to boxes of assorted chocolates,

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:41.667
10% are caramel, 10% are coconut,

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.300
and for some reason, the other 80% are "orange créme."

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:48.167
"Another one. Another one."

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:50.300
And finally, when it comes to single people

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.801
on Valentine's Day, 30% treat themselves to a nice meal,

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:56.067
30% spend time with their friends...

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.133
A lot of interesting data. [ Applause ]

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.934
Don't worry. Valentine's Day is almost over.

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:07.734
I saw that this Valentine's Day

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:09.567
Walmart was selling a Teddy bear

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:13.100
that you could give to someone to break up with them.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.367
-Ugh. -This is real. Here it is.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.734
This is a real -- Look at this.

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:18.000
-Ugh!

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.868
-T-shirt says "Bye bye!" on it.

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:23.033
There's also another one you can get, wearing a shirt

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:25.100
that says "Get your own Netflix account."

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.467
-Oh, my... -That's very interesting.

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:30.000
Meanwhile, today in Washington, First Lady Jill Biden

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.734
installed a massive Valentine to the country

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.400
on the North Lawn of the White House.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.300
Check -- Look at this thing. Yeah.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.434
Joe actually played with the dog for almost an hour

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.267
before realizing it was cardboard.

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:41.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:42.868
"Stay, Commander!"

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:45.667
[ Steve growls ]

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:46.834
"Good boy."

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.067
[ Steve growls, barks ]

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.767
Some political news.

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:52.167
Today former Trump cabinet member Nikki Haley

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:54.501
announced that she is running for president.

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:56.334
Yep, she served in Trump's cabinet,

00:02:56.334 --> 00:03:00.834
which is listed on her website in very, very small font.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:03.601
Yep, Haley was Trump's ambassador to the U.N.

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:06.400
She's the one who taught him that it's not pronounced "oon."

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:10.701
Some business news.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:13.267
For the first time, Amazon's self-driving car

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:16.467
transported passengers on public roads.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.801
The car drove perfectly, then they were thrown

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:21.801
on to their front porch like a cheap set of luggage.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.634
Whip!

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.467
Unfortunately, after the Amazon car

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:27.167
dropped one guy off at his doorstep,

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:28.534
someone ran up and stole him.

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:31.367
-Oh. -Terrible. Terrible story.

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:34.100
Speaking of cars, I heard that Hyundai and Kia

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.934
just rolled out a new software fix

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:38.534
that makes their cars harder to steal.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:41.634
Yeah, anti-stealing software is just a huge sign that says,

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.133
"This is a Kia."

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:44.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:46.534
And finally, in Las Vegas,

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.567
someone stole the catalytic converter...

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:50.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.000
...out of the Oscar Mayer Wienermobile.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:55.367
Right now, Oscar Mayer doesn't know whether

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:58.634
to call a mechanic, a butcher, or a urologist.

